::: section systems
## Systems map

I use personal projects as a vertical laboratory for understanding computation end to end rather than as isolated demos.

`models → inference → ML runtime → toolchains / VMs → operating system → hardware`

- **Models** — [Chris-GPT-2](https://github.com/christianrss/chris-gpt-2): pretraining, evaluation and reproducibility.
- **Inference** — [Chris-Llama](https://github.com/christianrss/chris-llama): GGUF, tokenization, attention, KV cache, quantization and CPU/GPU execution.
- **ML runtime** — [Chris-Torch](https://github.com/christianrss/chris-torch): tensors, autograd, neural-network components and accelerated backends.
- **Toolchains / VMs** — compiler, assembler, linker and virtual-machine experiments developed around ChrisOS.
- **Operating system** — [ChrisOS](https://github.com/christianrss/ChrisOS): kernel, memory, drivers, graphics, filesystems and low-level infrastructure.
- **Hardware** — electrical engineering, electronics and robotics as the physical layer beneath the software stack.

My professional work sits above and across this stack: enterprise systems, APIs, desktop and web applications, fiscal and retail software, infrastructure and internal engineering tools.
:::

::: section projects
## Selected projects

::: project period="2025 —" label="Operating systems"
### ChrisOS
An experimental x86-64 operating system and low-level playground for building kernels, memory management, drivers, graphics, filesystems, compilers, assemblers, linkers, virtual machines and emulation components from scratch.

**C · C++ · x86-64 · OSDev · Compilers**

[Source](https://github.com/christianrss/ChrisOS) · [Documentation](https://os.christiansoftware.org)
:::

::: project period="2026" label="LLM pretraining"
### Chris-GPT-2
A 124.5M-parameter GPT-2 trained from scratch on approximately 10B FineWeb-Edu tokens using 4× NVIDIA A100 GPUs, with reproducible training artifacts and SafeTensors/GGUF exports.

**Python · PyTorch · CUDA · NCCL · distributed training**

[Source](https://github.com/christianrss/chris-gpt-2) · [Model](https://huggingface.co/christianrss/chris-gpt-2-124m) · [GGUF](https://huggingface.co/christianrss/chris-gpt-2-124m-GGUF)
:::

::: project period="2026 —" label="LLM inference"
### Chris-Llama
An experimental LLM inference runtime in C for studying GGUF loading, tokenization, attention, KV cache, quantization, memory layout and CPU/GPU execution without hiding the implementation behind a large framework.

**C · GGUF · inference · quantization · CPU/GPU**

[Source](https://github.com/christianrss/chris-llama)
:::

::: project period="2026 —" label="Deep learning systems"
### Chris-Torch
A learning-oriented deep learning framework built from scratch with tensors, automatic differentiation, neural-network components, optimizers and accelerated execution backends.

**C++ · Python · autograd · neural networks · GPU**

[Source](https://github.com/christianrss/chris-torch)
:::

::: project period="2026 —" label="Computer science reference"
### Engineering Manual
An independent, bilingual reference for computer science and software engineering, covering foundational topics in data structures, algorithms, operating systems, databases and system design. Built with a static publishing pipeline, full-text search, structured learning tracks, editorial validation and automated deployment.

**Python · Jinja2 · Markdown · JavaScript · GitHub Actions**

[Read](https://manual.christiansoftware.org/en/) · [Source](https://github.com/christianrss/manual)
:::

::: project period="2026 —" label="Research platform"
### Marginal Thinking
An independent research platform on macroeconomics, markets, geopolitics, technology and global systems, with recurring reports, country research, structural datasets and primary-source analysis.

**Economics · data · research · publishing**

[Visit](https://marginalthinking.org/) · [Source](https://github.com/logicvisionai/marginalthinking)
:::

::: project period="2026 —" label="Market software"
### SharpEx
A market and portfolio-intelligence workspace combining multi-portfolio accounting, cross-asset data, digital assets, risk-adjusted analytics and structural research integration.

**JavaScript · Cloudflare Workers · market data · risk analytics**
:::
:::


::: section products
## Product engineering

These products demonstrate application architecture, real-time systems, local-first collaboration and desktop engineering. The links below contain public, architecture-level case studies; implementation and operational details remain private.

::: project period="2026 —" label="Local-first collaboration"
### Velis
Collaborative workspace for documents, tasks and team workflows. The architecture connects local persistence, multi-device synchronization and shared application services, balancing offline continuity with coordination.

**TypeScript · Web applications · Local-first systems · Collaboration**

[Product](https://velis.vu/) · [Architecture case study](/projects/en/velis/)
:::

::: project period="2026 —" label="Real-time media systems"
### Kaduo
Social-commerce and video platform combining a browser-based production studio, live video composition, media publication and playback with shopping experiences, creator tools and real-time audience participation.

**WebRTC · Browser media APIs · Canvas · TypeScript · Real-time applications**

[Product](https://kaduo.shop/) · [Architecture case study](/projects/en/kaduo/)
:::

::: project period="2026 —" label="Business SaaS"
### Eviz
Digital business identity and CRM SaaS connecting public-facing profiles and pages with lead capture, contact management and commercial workflows through modular application services.

**Web applications · SaaS · CRM · Relational data**

[Product](https://www.eviz.me/) · [Architecture case study](/projects/en/eviz/)
:::

::: project period="2026 —" label="Desktop and systems engineering"
### Chris Cleaner
Desktop utility focused on disk usage analysis, filesystem cataloging and user-controlled cleanup. Its architecture separates native system adapters, background processing, persistence and user-interface responsibilities.

**C# · .NET · Desktop software · Filesystems · Concurrency**

[Product website](https://christiansoftware.org/) · [Architecture case study](/projects/en/chris-cleaner/)
:::

::: project period="2026" label="Education platform"
### LOGV Learn
Learning platform for course publication, student progress and enrollment. The application separates learning content, identity, commercial access and learner experience as business domains.

**Next.js · TypeScript · Education platforms · Transactions**

[Architecture case study](/projects/en/logv-learn/)
:::
:::
::: section research
## Research & technical writing

::: entry period="2026" label="LLM training"
### A Reproducible 10-Billion-Token Pretraining Run of GPT-2 124M
Technical report covering the training setup, evaluation and reproducibility of the Chris-GPT-2 pretraining run.

[Paper](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/412096883_A_Reproducible_10-Billion-Token_Pretraining_Run_of_GPT-2_124M)
:::

::: entry period="2026" label="Model specialization"
### Specializing a 124M-Parameter GPT-2 for Linux
Study of continued pretraining and canonical instruction tuning for a Linux-focused GPT-2, including failure analysis.

[Paper](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/412275606_Specializing_a_124M-Parameter_GPT-2_for_Linux_Continued_Pretraining_Canonical_Instruction_Tuning_and_Failure_Analysis)
:::
:::

